{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the king of Egypt said, and he said to the midwives.</b> Twice ויאמר — on account of stylistic length. Or: the first ויאמר is the narration of the matter to the midwives; the second is an admonition and command to them that they do so. And the meaning of על האבנים המשבר: the place where the laboring woman kneels to give birth is called אבנים because the thighs of the woman in labor grow cold as stones, and similarly it is called משבר because her limbs are broken (משתברים), and so its Aramaic translation is מתברא. And the word האבנים may be read with the letter ה as two — ה בנים — and from this our Rabbis of blessed memory derived that six were in one womb. And further, the word האבנים alludes to the place of stones, which is the letter ה, the first ה in the Name, and I have already mentioned this regarding the verse (Genesis 38): ״והיה בכזיב״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The phrase על האבנים המשבר in the lemma appears to combine elements from Exodus 1:16 (על האבנים) with a word (משבר) drawn from the explanation that follows; rendered as the commentary presents it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:07.205777763Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}